Our pipeline begins by reconstructing (a) a cloth-extended SMPLX mesh with aligned Gaussian textures. To address complex dynamic non-rigid deformations, (b) we employ a teacher StyleUnet to learn pose-dependent non-rigid maps, which are then baked into a lightweight student MLP to infer non-rigid deformations of our template mesh. For high-fidelity rendering, (c) we introduce learnable Gaussian blend shapes to enhance appearance details.}
    \label{fig:method}
