\subsection{Cube-stream structure} 

% In early studies, a single region and single-satellite sample with dimensions of $\mathbb{R}^{H \times W \times C}$ was typically used to describe marine fog, where $H, W, B$ represents height, width and the number of bands detected by satellite imager, respectively. However, 

