To address two primary challenges discussed in Section~\ref{sec:intro}, we propose \method:
\textbf{1)} We propose using pseudo-labels to approximate training dynamic scores, and we employ deep clustering to generate pseudo-labels~\citep{adaloglou2023exploring} (Section~\ref{ssec:coreset-pseudo}).
\textbf{2)} We find that simply using existing sampling algorithms tends to choose too many easy examples, which leads to inferior performance. 
We propose a simple but effective double-end pruning algorithm to mitigate this bias. 
The pipeline of ELFS is illustrated in Figure~\ref{fig:deepclustering_pipeline}.

