\subsection{Scene-Adaptive Loss Function}
The key benefit of sensor fusion in this work is that the shortcomings of one sensor can be overcome by relying on information from the other  (\cref{fig:strengths_figure}). In order to adaptively do so during optimization, we quantify the ``usefulness'' of information available in the RGB image. The loss function will use this quantification of usefulness to adaptively determine whether to rely on the RGB or LiDAR image more.

% We can take advantage of the first benefit by simply summing the RGB and LiDAR loss

