\section{Multi-view Video Synthesis via SV4D 2.0}
\vspace{-2mm}


SV4D 2.0 generates dynamic 3D content by first synthesizing multiple novel-view videos given a monocular video as input then optimizing a 4D representation via photogrammetry. 
Similar to SV4D~\cite{xie2024sv4d}, we leverage the temporal prior in a video diffusion model as well as the 3D prior in a multi-view diffusion model, while introducing key improvements in both multi-view video synthesis and 4D optimization.


