% The advantage of using a hypernetwork, rather than directly regressing activations from the transformer, lies in its ability to decouple context understanding from the prediction mechanism. This structure enables more flexible task adaptation, improved interpretability, and controllable downstream components. Moreover, it supports reusability of the encoder architecture and modular fine-tuning for different regions or subjects.
