This process is illustrated in the top right of \cref{fig:stage_i_fig}.

\noindent
\textbf{Summary for Stage-I.}
The final objective for Stage-I is to minimize the sum of \textbf{global} and \textbf{fine-grained} aligning losses, balanced by a trade-off coefficient, $\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm I}=\gamma \mathcal{L}_g + (1-\gamma)\mathcal{L}_f$.
Note that during this adaptation process, the CLIP-Text encoder model remains frozen, and only the CLIP-Vision encoder is fine-tuned. Our fine-grained frame-AD matching is entirely parameter-free, as only the vision encoder will be utilized in the subsequent stage.


